10-What are Scrum artifacts and events? Explain how the Product Backlog, Sprint Backlog, Increment, Sprint, Daily Scrum, Sprint Review, and Sprint Retrospective contribute to a project.
Answer 10: Scrum artifacts are important information used to plan and track the work. Scrum events are activities where the team plans, discusses, reviews, and improves their work.
Product Backlog: It contains all the work and features that need to be completed for the product.
Sprint Backlog: It contains the tasks selected for the current Sprint and helps the Developers focus on their work.
Increment: It is the completed and usable part of the product delivered at the end of a Sprint.
Sprint: It is a fixed period when the Scrum Team works together to achieve a specific goal and deliver an Increment.
Sprint planning: A meeting whre the team plans for the upcoming sprint.
Daily Scrum: It is a short daily meeting where Developers discuss progress and plan their work for the day.
Sprint Review: It is a meeting where the team shows the completed work, receives feedback, and discusses what to do next.
Sprint Retrospective: It is a meeting where the team discusses what went well, what could be improved, and how to work better in the next Sprint.


